  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06XA">Lemma <span data-tag="06XA">96.19.3</span>.</a> If there exists a $1$-morphism $s : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{U}$ such that $f \circ s$ is $2$-isomorphic to $\text{id}_\mathcal {X}$ then the extended relative Čech complex is homotopic to zero. </p>
